cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use paftacular in research, please cite the software using this metadata."
title: "paftacular: Parsing and serializing mzPAF peak annotations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Garrett
    given-names: Patrick
    affiliation: Scripps Research
    email: pgarrett@scripps.edu
abstract: >-
  paftacular is a Python library for parsing, constructing, serializing, and
  analyzing HUPO Proteomics Standards Initiative mzPAF peak annotations. It
  supports fragment-ion types, modifications, isotopes, adducts, charge states,
  mass errors, confidence scores, and mass and elemental-composition calculations.
keywords:
  - mass spectrometry
  - mzPAF
  - peak annotation
  - proteomics
  - HUPO-PSI
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tacular-omics/paftacular"
url: "https://paftacular.readthedocs.io/"
version: 1.1.1
date-released: 2026-08-15
